1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,140
[Prof. Peter Kim] On Slide 29, we examine the cutting edge of autonomous commerce: AP2, the Agent Payments Protocol.

2
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:15,500
[TA Sarah Jenkins] AP2 is the open standard that allows AI agents to buy goods and subscribe to services safely on our behalf.

3
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:29,920
[Prof. Peter Kim] Pillar 1 is the Scoped Mandate. Instead of handing over a credit card number, the user issues a cryptographically signed token that says: "You may spend up to $25 exclusively at merchant X for item Y."

4
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:37,930
[TA Sarah Jenkins] Pillar 2 uses Zero-Knowledge Proofs. The merchant never sees your personal banking info, preventing data leaks.

5
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:46,990
[Prof. Peter Kim] And Pillar 3 is Reversible Escrow. The funds are held in escrow until the software delivers valid proof of completion.

6
00:00:47,390 --> 00:00:50,870
[TA Sarah Jenkins] This is the future of the autonomous agent economy.

